To create a simple web page using HTML and CSS, follow these steps:

1. Set up the HTML structure:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>My First Web Page</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <h1>Welcome to My First Web Page!</h1>
    </header>
    <main>
        <p>This is a simple web page created using HTML and CSS.</p>
        <p>You can customize the design by editing the styles.css file.</p>
    </main>
    <footer>
        <p>© 2022 My First Web Page</p>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
```

2. Create the CSS file (styles.css):

```css
body {
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
}

header {
    background-color: #f8f9fa;
    padding: 20px;
    text-align: center;
}

main {
    padding: 0 20px;
}

footer {
    background-color: #f8f9fa;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 10px;
    position: fixed;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 100%;
}
```

3. Save both files in the same directory, then open the HTML file in a web browser to see your web page.

This example creates a simple web page with a header, main content, and footer. The CSS file is linked to the HTML file, allowing you to customize the design easily. The body text uses the Arial font, and each section has some basic styling applied. The footer is positioned at the bottom of the page using CSS positioning.
